    "content": "# Grade: C\n\n## Requirement checks\n\n- MCP catalog entry read: Satisfied by the supplied MCP result.\n- Defines `func add(a, b)`: Satisfied.\n- Returns `a + b`: Semantically satisfied.\n- Calls `print(add(2, 3))`: Satisfied.\n- Returns only the script: Satisfied by the draft.\n- Execution status: Not executed.\n\n## Correctness concerns\n\nThe draft omits Kujo statement terminators. Based on the supplied syntax, `return a + b` should end with `;`, the function declaration with `;`, and the `print` call with `;`. Without execution, whether newlines are accepted as substitutes remains uncertain.\n\n## Suggested corrections\n\n```kujo\nfunc add(a, b) {\n  return a + b;\n};\n\nprint(add(2, 3));\n```",
